+
+# Implement RFC 7386 JSON Merge Patch applyMergePatch
+
+## Request
+
+Some clients send partial updates in JSON Merge Patch format. Implement JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386):
+export `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` from `src/index.ts`, which applies a merge patch to a target
+JSON document and returns the merged document.
+
+## Done
+
+- `src/json-merge-patch.ts`: `applyMergePatch` (RFC 7386 section 2 algorithm, applied to deep copies of
+  both inputs) and `JsonMergePatchError`; both exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- `src/json-value.ts`: `cloneJson`, `isPlainObject` and `setMember` moved out of `src/json-patch.ts`
+  (unchanged, except that the internal error class is now `JsonValueError`), so both features validate
+  JSON values the same way. The 64 existing tests still pass.
+- `test/apply-merge-patch.test.ts`: 35 tests, red first (all failed before the implementation, since
+  the export did not exist): every RFC 7386 appendix A example and the section 3 example; removing a
+  missing member; non-object targets; `null` inside arrays; inputs never modified and not shared;
+  `__proto__` and inherited members; non-JSON values, cycles, throwing getters and over-deep values
+  rejected as `JsonMergePatchError`. 99 tests pass.
+- `README.md`: JSON Merge Patch section.
+- Decision: dl-005 (copy-on-apply, strict JSON inputs, JsonMergePatchError).
+
+## Notes
+
+- dl-003 and dl-004 (JSON Patch) are still pending approval; dl-005 reuses their validation rules.
+- `tsc` is not installed, so type-checking was not run; no coverage threshold is declared.
